<title>GERMANY: Zeitler - French poll move shows will for timely EMU. [CORRECTED 09:52 GMT]</title>
<headline>Zeitler - French poll move shows will for timely EMU. [CORRECTED 09:52 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Franz-Christoph Zeitler said on Tuesday that the decision by French President Jacques Chirac to hold early elections showed a clear will to join European economic and monetary union (EMU) on time in 1999.</p>
<p>But responding to a question on whether Germany might make a similar move, Zeitler made it clear that he thought this was unlikely. Germany is due to hold elections in the autumn of 1998.</p>
<p>France's Chirac dissolved his country's National Assembly late on Monday and called a parliamentary election for May 25 (corrects from May 15) and June 1.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 7565 1246</p>
</text>
